From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kitty Crow <https://kittycrow.dev>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Linux-WASM hush on the parent terminal

Linux-WASM runs inside a host process which already owns the terminal. BusyBox
hush job control hands that terminal to each child process with tcsetpgrp(), but
the WebAssembly process boundary does not reliably hand it back. The host shell
then becomes foreground while the guest shell remains alive.

Keep HUSH_JOB compiled because the upstream Linux-WASM BusyBox build expects
that feature layout, but suppress child process-group terminal handoff for Wasm.
---
 shell/hush.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shell/hush.c b/shell/hush.c
index c634ffa..1111111 100644
--- a/shell/hush.c
+++ b/shell/hush.c
@@ -9244,6 +9244,13 @@ static int run_pipe_child(void *arg) {
 	/* Every child adds itself to new process group
 		* with pgid == pid_of_first_child_in_pipe */
+#if defined(__wasm__)
+	/*
+	 * The host process owns the terminal. Moving it to a guest child process
+	 * leaves the host shell in the foreground after that child exits because
+	 * the Linux-WASM boundary cannot reliably restore the guest shell pgrp.
+	 */
+	if (0) {
+#else
 	if (G.run_list_level == 1 && G_interactive_fd) {
+#endif
 		pid_t pgrp;
 		pgrp = pi->pgrp;
 		if (pgrp < 0) /* true for 1st process only */
